Package: quota-dock
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Quota Dock contributors <noreply@localhost>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-venv, python3-tk, xkb-data, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libxcb-cursor0, libegl1, libgl1, libdbus-1-3, libfontconfig1, libx11-xcb1, libwayland-client0, libwayland-cursor0, libwayland-egl1, libxcb-icccm4, libxcb-keysyms1, libxcb-shape0, libxcb-xinerama0, libxcb-render-util0, libxcb-randr0, libxcb-xfixes0, libxcb-sync1, libxcb-xkb1
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core, libnotify-bin
Description: Desktop widget for Codex and Claude subscription usage
 Shows observed weekly usage, reset times and recovery notifications.
 The first launch opens a preparation window and downloads PySide6 into
 an isolated environment for the logged-in user. An internet connection
 is required for that preparation. No system Python packages are changed.
 Codex and Claude Code must be installed and signed in separately.
 Designed for Ubuntu 22.04, 24.04 and 26.04 desktop sessions.
